<title>PERU: TABLE - Peru's H1 trade deficit falls 48 percent.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Peru's H1 trade deficit falls 48 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a breakdown of Peruvian foreign trade figures for the first half of the year, released Friday by the Central Reserve Bank:</p>
<p>			   1997		   1996</p>
<p>Jan-June</p>
<p>    Exports	   3,445		   2,886</p>
<p>    Imports	   3,920		   3,802</p>
<p>    Balance	   (475)		   (916)</p>
<p>NOTES:</p>
<p>-- All figures in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>-- Peru's trade deficit fell nine percent in 1996 to $1.996 billion from $2.185 billion in 1995, according to the Central Reserve Bank.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
</text>
